=== pressure ===
The contradictions do not make people more honest. They make them more specific.

* [Press Arin on the pharmacy purchase]
    ~ discover_evidence("pharmacy_footage")
    ARIN: It was for a column. People eat poisonous things all the time. Usually on purpose.
    -> reconstruction
* [Show Mira the receipt]
    ~ record_statement("mira_left_1910")
    MIRA: Fine. I was still here. That does not make me the person who killed him.
    -> reconstruction
* [Stop asking questions]
    -> reconstruction
* [Read the café records]
    -> paperwork
* [Begin second interviews]
    -> second_interview
* [Open the motive file]
    -> reconstruct_motive
* [Open the late interview file]
    -> late_interview

=== paperwork ===
The useful parts of a case rarely arrive with useful labels. They arrive as a receipt folded into a wallet, a message archived under a joke, or a person saying "I don't remember" with exact confidence.

You lay the café records across the table. The ink on the till roll is fading in the middle, where the receipt matters most.

* [Compare Mira's card number]
    Receipt \#004 ends in 4412. Mira's manager card ends in 4412. The card was in her wallet when you asked. That makes the purchase hers, not necessarily her hand's.
    -> paperwork
* [Read the camera maintenance note]
    The west camera has failed twice this month. Both failures happened after Jo cleaned the panel. A recurring failure is an explanation. It is not an alibi.
    -> paperwork
* [Read the staff group chat]
    At 19:17, Jo wrote: "screen is doing the thing again." At 19:31, Mira wrote: "nobody touch the west panel." The messages make the outage less mysterious and Jo less comfortable.
    -> paperwork
* [Ask what remains unexplained]
    The camera gap explains why nobody can place a hand on the cup. It does not explain why aconite was purchased twenty-two minutes before the death window.
    -> paperwork
* [Move to the second interviews]
    -> late_interview
* [Read Eli's background file]
    -> backstory
* [Return to the reconstruction]
    -> reconstruction

=== second_interview ===
Everyone has now heard that the camera was broken. The first round of answers has become a collection of small edits.

* [Ask Mira about her card]
    MIRA: I manage the café. I use the café card. It is not a confession to be financially boring.
    You ask why she first said she left at 19:10.
    MIRA: Because Eli was there, and I did not want you asking why.
    -> second_interview
* [Ask Arin about the paper bag]
    ARIN: You are very interested in a bag.
    You are more interested in the bottle it carried.
    ARIN: I bought something for an article. The article was going to be about bad wellness advice. It was not going to be about Eli.
    -> second_interview
* [Ask Jo whether she saw a face]
    JO: No. I saw a shoulder, a cup, and somebody moving as if the floor belonged to them.
    You ask if that sounds like Arin.
    JO: It sounds like a person who has been in the room before.
    -> second_interview
* [Ask Sasha why the key mattered]
    SASHA: Eli kept the café key because he liked having a reason to call me. I came to take it back.
    You ask if she found it.
    SASHA: No. I found him dead instead. I would prefer the key.
    -> second_interview
* [Ask Dan about the missing route]
    DAN: The delivery app drew a line through a building. I followed the line, not the building.
    You ask if he saw Arin.
    DAN: I saw a paper bag. Everyone in this part of town has a paper bag.
    -> second_interview
* [Return to the records]
    -> paperwork

=== backstory ===
Eli Venn was good at finding the soft place in a person and pressing it with one finger. He called this curiosity. The people around him called it different things depending on whether they were still being invited to dinner.

The café had given him a corner table because he paid on time and tipped in cash. Mira gave him the table because he had once helped her negotiate a lease. Jo gave him coffee because it was her job. Sasha gave him a key because she thought a relationship could survive a practical arrangement. Arin gave him material because an editor needed a name.

None of those transactions is a murder motive by itself. Together they describe a room in which every person had been made to feel observed.

* [Ask why Eli kept records]
    Eli wrote down dates and phrases in a small black notebook. He liked the feeling of being the only person who could remember a conversation correctly.
    -> backstory
* [Ask who feared the notebook]
    Mira feared the pages about her. Arin feared the pages about his work. Sasha feared nothing in the notebook as much as she feared the debt list in Eli's phone.
    -> backstory
* [Ask what Jo remembers]
    Jo remembers that Eli never finished an iced drink. He drank half, left the straw crooked, and asked for the receipt even when he had not paid.
    -> backstory
* [Ask what Dan remembers]
    Dan remembers the blue dish by the till and the bell above the service door. He remembers the room because delivery work is mostly remembering rooms.
    -> backstory
* [Open the physical evidence]
    -> reconstruction
